#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:8
msgid "About ROS"
msgstr "關於 ROS"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:10
msgid ""
"ROS (Robot Operating System) is an open-source ecosystem that provides the "
"framework, tools, and libraries for building, deploying, running, and "
"maintaining robotic applications. This article introduces the main areas of "
"the ecosystem and outlines their intended use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:13
msgid ""
"**Area: ROS-framework, ROS-tools, ROS-capabilities | Content-type: about | "
"Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:17
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr "目次表"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:20
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "摘要"

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:22
msgid ""
"ROS is used in many areas of robotics. In logistics, it helps robots move "
"goods in warehouses by providing navigation, mapping, motion control, and "
"coordination between multiple robots. In manufacturing, it enables advanced "
"tasks such as automated pick-and-place operations using vision systems for "
"accurate handling. In healthcare, ROS supports robotic systems that assist "
"with patient care and improve efficiency in clinical workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:27
msgid "Watch the `ROS video`_ for a quick introduction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:32
msgid "The ecosystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:34
msgid ""
"Despite its name, ROS is actually not an operating system in the traditional "
"sense, but a set of tools and libraries that help developers create robots "
"using various platforms and programming languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:36
msgid "Animated high level diagram of the ROS ecosystem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:40
msgid "Framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:42
msgid ""
"The ROS framework is the “plumbing” which allows for communication between "
"parts of a robot, and within parts of a robot. It includes messaging, "
"standard interfaces, and support for multiple programming languages and "
"platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:45
msgid ""
"For example, the framework handles sending data from a camera to a "
"processing node or passing commands from a planning system to a motor "
"controller. It also provides the structure for sharing software across "
"systems, so developers can build modular and reusable solutions."
msgstr ""

