#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:76
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:78
msgid ""
"Capabilities in ROS are ready-to-use packages that offer common functions "
"for robots, such as manipulation, motion planning, and perception. These "
"packages allow developers to add advanced behaviours without starting from "
"scratch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:81
msgid ""
"For example, manipulation packages can control robotic arms for tasks like "
"picking and placing objects in automated workflows. Motion planning packages "
"allow robots to move from one point to another by calculating safe paths in "
"their environment. Perception packages enable robots to detect and recognise "
"objects or people, supporting tasks such as retrieving objects or working in "
"environments where the robot needs to respond to what it sees. Different "
"implementations of the same capabilities allow developers to switch "
"implementations and experiment to find the best implementation for their "
"needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:87
msgid ""
"Apart from the packages maintained by Open Robotics, you can also choose "
"from many packages contributed by the ROS community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:89
msgid ""
"ROS offers the following core capabilities either out of the box, or through "
"supported third-party solutions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:91
msgid "Simulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:92
msgid "Motion planning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:93
msgid "Navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/About-ROS/About-ROS.rst:94
msgid "Manipulation"
msgstr ""

